hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"886","919 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yala narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he praised Allah and extolled Him, admonished and reminded, and said: To proceed, the prohibition of wine came down on the day it came down, and it is from five: from grapes, dates, wheat, barley, and honey. And wine is whatever covers the intellect."
"887","920 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When wine was prohibited we said: O Messenger of Allah, we have wine belonging to an orphan. So he ordered us and we poured it out."
"888","921 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Qabisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Hubayra, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wine being made into vinegar, and he disliked it."
"889","922 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful."
"890","923 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Qurra, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have drinks - or a drink - from this bit made of honey, and mizr made of corn and barley; what do you command us? He said: I forbid you every intoxicant."
"891","924 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is unlawful."
"892","925 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - he is Ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping in the muqayyar, the muzaffat, the dubba, the hantama, and the naqir. He said: And every intoxicant is unlawful."
"893","926 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"894","927 - Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, he said: Abu Damra narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Bakr ibn Abi al-Furat, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"895","928 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed me, he said: Abu Uthman al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in the amount of a faraq, a handful of it is unlawful."
"896","929 - Sad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam and Allan ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, they said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed me, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I forbid you the small amount of whatever intoxicates in large amount."
"897","930 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them, for Muhammad was permitted to visit his mother, and it reminds of the Hereafter. And I forbade you keeping the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, intending thereby that the well-off widen upon those without means; so eat and store. And I forbade you vessels, though a vessel neither makes anything lawful nor unlawful. And every intoxicant is unlawful."
"898","931 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade unripe dates and ripe dates being mixed together, and raisins and dates being mixed together; and he wrote to the people of Jurash not to mix raisins and dates."
"899","932 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla; and Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Layla; and Abu Farwa, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: Hudhayfa, may Allah be pleased with him, asked for drink, so a dihqan brought him water in a silver vessel and he threw it aside, then excused himself to them for what he did and said: I had forbidden him; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not drink in vessels of gold and silver, nor wear dibaj nor silk; for they are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter."
"900","933 - Abu Jafar al-Mukharrami, Ishaq ibn Mansur, and Umar ibn Shabba narrated to us - and the hadith is that of Abu Jafar - they said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shuba, who said: Qatada narrated to me, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Said al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man drinking while standing."
"901","934 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Hudayr informed me, from Yazid ibn Utarid Abu al-Bazari, who said: I asked Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, about drinking while standing, and he said: We used to drink while standing, and eat while walking, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"902","935 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik, from al-Bara ibn Zayd, son of the daughter of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that his mother reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her while a waterskin was hanging, and drank from the mouth of the skin standing. She said: So I stood to it and cut it off."
